---
import { ArrowLeft, ExternalLink } from "@lucide/astro";

import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

export const prerender = true;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Case Study A | TrialDiff"
  description="A clean in-corpus TrialDiff case study showing how to read an Evidence Record."
>
  <main class="page-shell stack methodology-page" id="main-content">
    <a class="button" href="/">
      <ArrowLeft size={16} aria-hidden="true" />
      Back to dashboard
    </a>

    <header class="panel panel-pad">
      <p class="eyebrow">Case Study A</p>
      <h1>How to read an Evidence Record</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This case uses an in-corpus secondary-outcome record from NCT01441947. It is a compact mechanism demo: five
        changed paths, one outcome rule, one timing modifier, and explicit claim boundaries.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="panel panel-pad disclaimer">
      <div class="disclaimer-inner">
        <div>
          Severity is deterministic, reproducible, uncalibrated triage metadata, not validated review priority or proven wrongdoing. This case study explains what the registry record supports and what it does not support.
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="panel panel-pad method-section">
      <h2>Record</h2>
      <p>
        TrialDiff compares ClinicalTrials.gov versions 16 and 17 for NCT01441947, a Massachusetts General Hospital
        study titled "Cabozantinib in Women With Metastatic Hormone-Receptor-Positive Breast Cancer."
      </p>
      <p>
        Evidence Record:
        <a href="/events/evt_NCT01441947_v16_v17_1493ccf4a7cd">
          evt_NCT01441947_v16_v17_1493ccf4a7cd
        </a>
      </p>
      <p>
        Canonical JSON:
        <a href="/events/evt_NCT01441947_v16_v17_1493ccf4a7cd.json">
          /events/evt_NCT01441947_v16_v17_1493ccf4a7cd.json
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel panel-pad method-section">
      <h2>What Changed</h2>
      <p>
        The patch removed one path under the secondary-outcome module:
        <code>/protocolSection/outcomesModule/secondaryOutcomes/3</code>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The same amendment also updated registry housekeeping paths including status verification date, last update
        submit date, and last update post date. It also added an annotation section. The case is useful because the
        evidence object is small enough to inspect directly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel panel-pad method-section">
      <h2>Why It Carried The Critical Triage Label</h2>
      <p>
        The deterministic rule <code>secondary_outcome_any_change</code> fired because a secondary-outcome registry path
        changed. The base triage severity was high.
      </p>
      <p>
        The from-version timing context was <code>late_recruitment</code>. TrialDiff's timing modifier escalated the
        final triage severity from high to critical because late-stage outcome changes have a higher triage label than the
        same change before recruitment.
      </p>
      <p>
        This section describes the classifier output, not an independent validation that critical is the correct review-priority tier. v0.2.1 calibration failed, so severity is retained only as uncalibrated triage metadata.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel panel-pad method-section">
      <h2>What This Supports</h2>
      <p>
        This record supports a narrow factual statement: a secondary-outcome registry field changed between versions 16
        and 17, the change occurred in a late-recruitment context, and the stored JSON Patch and rule hash identify why
        TrialDiff assigned it a deterministic triage label.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel panel-pad method-section">
      <h2>What This Does Not Support</h2>
      <p>
        This case does not show misconduct, sponsor intent, scientific unjustifiability, manuscript non-disclosure, or
        regulatory non-compliance. It also does not determine whether the registry outcome change reflects outcome
        switching rather than a legitimate registry correction.
      </p>
      <p>
        The correct next question is the record's own review question: what did the secondary outcome field say before
        and after the amendment, and what contemporaneous public document explains the change?
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel panel-pad method-section">
      <h2>External Source</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01441947">
          View NCT01441947 on ClinicalTrials.gov
          <ExternalLink size={14} aria-hidden="true" />
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
